  {
   "id": "text_not_engineered",
   "file": "src/RimMandrake/Pyrelands/Defs/BiomeDefs/Pyrelands.xml",
   "old": "<description>A hot, wind-scoured savanna, genetically engineered in a forgotten age to feed grazing herds, that has gone on burning on a schedule of its own for millennia. Coarse fast grass carpets the ground again within days of a burn, dries out soon after, and goes up at the first dry-storm strike. What is left behind is ash: drifting on every wind, falling in grey storms, banking into drifts, and lying deep over all of it. Dry, the ash is fair ground that takes a crop well enough, though the heat stunts it; wherever water reaches it, the ash turns very fertile, wet roots shrug off the heat and it grows almost anything. For a few days after a burn the ash itself feeds a field, and black rain on a fresh burn feeds it richer still. The rare rain here is black with it. Little grows tall enough to matter, so the horizon is nothing but grass, scars and smoke.</description>",
   "new": "<description>A hot, wind-scoured savanna, natural in a forgotten age to feed grazing herds, that has gone on burning on a schedule of its own for millennia. Coarse fast grass carpets the ground again within days of a burn, dries out soon after, and goes up at the first dry-storm strike. What is left behind is ash: drifting on every wind, falling in grey storms, banking into drifts, and lying deep over all of it. Dry, the ash is fair ground that takes a crop well enough, though the heat stunts it; wherever water reaches it, the ash turns very fertile, wet roots shrug off the heat and it grows almost anything. For a few days after a burn the ash itself feeds a field, and black rain on a fresh burn feeds it richer still. The rare rain here is black with it. Little grows tall enough to matter, so the horizon is nothing but grass, scars and smoke.</description>",
   "bars": [
    "biome_text_says_engineered"
   ],
   "suites": [
